<!--
    Chart/summary metadata for the FitContributor fields created in
    ActivityController.mc (session.createField() ids must match these).
    Without this, sideloaded builds still write the fields into the FIT
    file correctly (confirmed via FitCSVTool), but tools that visualize
    FitContributor data, such as MonkeyGraph and Garmin Connect once/if
    this app is published to the store, have no chart/label config to
    render them with.

    hr_zone_seconds (id 0) is a 5 element array (seconds per HR zone for
    the whole session), so displayInChart is a reasonable fit, since it's
    inherently a small multi value breakdown, not a single scalar.

    grade_percent/grade_adjusted_speed (ids 1/2) are MESG_TYPE_RECORD,
    charted per-second values, not session totals. These exist to build up
    a dataset (grade, speed, HR all recorded per-second) for tuning the
    gradeAdjustCoefficient app setting from real rides, not because the
    current coefficient is known to be correct.

    skate_seconds/other_seconds (ids 3/4) are each a single cumulative
    total for the whole session, tagged manually via the Up/Down buttons
    (see FreeskateDelegate.mc) rather than auto-detected, so
    displayInActivitySummary (a plain summary stat) fits them better than
    displayInChart, which implies plotting a value over time and doesn't
    apply here since there's only one final value per session.

    lap_skate_distance (id 5) is MESG_TYPE_LAP in code, reset every lap,
    so displayInActivityLaps shows it as a per-lap breakdown rather than
    one session total.

    skate_speed/walk_speed (ids 6/7) are MESG_TYPE_RECORD (written every
    second), each nonzero only in its own tagged state and zero otherwise.
    Both charted, in different colors, as an approximation of a single
    color-coded speed graph, since Garmin Connect's built-in Speed chart
    has no customization hook for third-party developer fields, so this
    is a separate pair of charts rather than a literal recoloring of
    that one.

    regular_seconds/goofy_seconds (ids 8/9) mirror skate_seconds/
    other_seconds (id 3/4): a single cumulative total for the whole
    session, tagged manually via the pause-menu ToggleMenuItem (see
    PauseMenuDelegate.mc) rather than auto-detected, so
    displayInActivitySummary fits them the same way. Only accumulate while
    also tagged skating; stance doesn't apply to the walking tag.

    regular_speed/goofy_speed (ids 10/11) mirror skate_speed/walk_speed
    (id 6/7): MESG_TYPE_RECORD, each nonzero only while tagged skating AND
    that stance, zero otherwise, charted as the same kind of color-coded
    speed-graph approximation.

    pump_cadence (id 12) is MESG_TYPE_RECORD, written every second by
    PumpCadenceDetector via ActivityController: a wrist-accelerometer-
    derived estimate of pumping cycles per minute, zero while tagged
    walking. Charted like grade_percent/grade_adjusted_speed: the point
    right now is building up a dataset to look at from real rides, since
    the detector's peak threshold is an unvalidated starting guess.
-->
<resources xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://developer.garmin.com/downloads/connect-iq/resources.xsd">
    <fitContributions>
        <fitField id="0"
            displayInChart="true"
            sortOrder="0"
            precision="0"
            chartTitle="@Strings.HrZoneSecondsLabel"
            dataLabel="@Strings.HrZoneSecondsLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SecondsUnit"
            fillColor="#FF8800" />
        <fitField id="1"
            displayInChart="true"
            sortOrder="1"
            precision="1"
            chartTitle="@Strings.GradePercentLabel"
            dataLabel="@Strings.GradePercentLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.PercentUnit"
            fillColor="#0088FF" />
        <fitField id="2"
            displayInChart="true"
            sortOrder="2"
            precision="1"
            chartTitle="@Strings.GradeAdjustedSpeedLabel"
            dataLabel="@Strings.GradeAdjustedSpeedLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SpeedUnit"
            fillColor="#CC00CC" />
        <fitField id="3"
            displayInActivitySummary="true"
            sortOrder="3"
            precision="0"
            dataLabel="@Strings.SkateSecondsLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SecondsUnit" />
        <fitField id="4"
            displayInActivitySummary="true"
            sortOrder="4"
            precision="0"
            dataLabel="@Strings.OtherSecondsLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SecondsUnit" />
        <fitField id="5"
            displayInActivityLaps="true"
            sortOrder="5"
            precision="0"
            dataLabel="@Strings.LapSkateDistanceLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.MetersUnit" />
        <fitField id="6"
            displayInChart="true"
            sortOrder="6"
            precision="1"
            chartTitle="@Strings.SkateSpeedLabel"
            dataLabel="@Strings.SkateSpeedLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SpeedUnit"
            fillColor="#00CC00" />
        <fitField id="7"
            displayInChart="true"
            sortOrder="7"
            precision="1"
            chartTitle="@Strings.WalkSpeedLabel"
            dataLabel="@Strings.WalkSpeedLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SpeedUnit"
            fillColor="#888888" />
        <fitField id="8"
            displayInActivitySummary="true"
            sortOrder="8"
            precision="0"
            dataLabel="@Strings.RegularSecondsLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SecondsUnit" />
        <fitField id="9"
            displayInActivitySummary="true"
            sortOrder="9"
            precision="0"
            dataLabel="@Strings.GoofySecondsLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SecondsUnit" />
        <fitField id="10"
            displayInChart="true"
            sortOrder="10"
            precision="1"
            chartTitle="@Strings.RegularSpeedLabel"
            dataLabel="@Strings.RegularSpeedLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SpeedUnit"
            fillColor="#0044CC" />
        <fitField id="11"
            displayInChart="true"
            sortOrder="11"
            precision="1"
            chartTitle="@Strings.GoofySpeedLabel"
            dataLabel="@Strings.GoofySpeedLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SpeedUnit"
            fillColor="#CC8800" />
        <fitField id="12"
            displayInChart="true"
            sortOrder="12"
            precision="0"
            chartTitle="@Strings.PumpCadenceLabel"
            dataLabel="@Strings.PumpCadenceLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.CadenceUnit"
            fillColor="#00CCCC" />
    </fitContributions>
</resources>
